hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another video usually needs videos I  talk about famous entrepreneurs and the  lessons that you can learn from their  success today I'm gonna take a slightly  different approach and I'm going to talk  about my iPad I just came back from a  vacation and I use my iPad as my main  computing device instead of bringing my  computer and it save might be patient I  want to talk about all the different  ways that I used it and hopefully tell  you about a couple apps that you haven't  heard of and how you might be able to  use it for your next trip as well so  here we go app number one DJ or iPod  driving from Toronto to New York is  about a nine hour trip depending on  delays at the border  they can get really boring if you don't  have music my wife and I have a  tradition of making a new CD full of  songs every time we travel unfortunately  once we crossing the Buffalo we stopped  at a Plaza and I loved the car lights on  I killed our battery we got a new  battery installed that our stereo system  has an anti-theft mechanism that if you  change the battery the stereo gets  disabled unless you have the unlock code  we didn't have an honest which meant no  music for the rest of our trip enter DJ  or iPod luckily I had loaded my songs  onto my iPad as well before we left we  had music for the rest of our trip the  iPad batteries were awesome and the  speaker was pretty good in the car we  found the best spot to put the iPad was  in the Sun Visor with a speaker pointing  down I bought the DJ app because I'm  also a salsa DJ in my part time it's the  best app I know that I've seen for  mixing songs and hosting parties but the  native iPod app would have done the  trick just as well and it's free  app number two evernote evernote is a  cool tool that lets you store notes and  pictures online and access them from any  device i've used in the past to go  paperless and get rid of all my paper  receipts and after watch the video on  youtube I never really use it for  anything beyond keeping track of my  receipts but this vacation provided a  perfect opportunity to test it out  before going away I loaded my desktop  version of Evernote with information on  each city that would be visited I put in  places we should visit information about  where we would be docking and a little  bit of history about the city it  automatically synced with my Evernote  app on my iPad and whenever we landed in  a new city I had all the information at  my fingertips the basic app is free but  if you want to be able to have the  information available offline then you  need to upgrade for $4.99 a month of  $44.99 in a year I know some  entrepreneurs who store every idea they  have on Evernote and use it as an  integral part of their business I'll  definitely be looking at other ways to  incorporate it into my daily life after  the great experience from this trip app  number three  sleep pillow my son is a little over two  years old and is used to sleeping with  the sound machine that helps drown out  any background noise unfortunately in  our haste to leave  we forgot his sound machine at home  there must be an app for that  enter sleep pillow with this app you can  choose from a large selection of sounds  to help you fall asleep from water  falling the chimes to spa music our  favorite was the electric fan it were  like a charm and when you're traveling  with the two-year-old nothing beats a  good night's sleep  app number four male when you're  traveling on a cruise ship connecting to  the Internet can cost upwards of $1 per  minute in the past my wife and I would  connect using Microsoft Outlook download  our emails disconnect respond to the  emails reconnect and send so we're not  spending hundreds of dollars on slow  cruise ship Wi-Fi this time I took a  different approach I connected my email  to my iPad and when we landed in a new  city would find a local Starbucks and  connect to download my email after  dinner back onboard the ship  I would load up the emails respond and  the next day connect again in a new city  to send the emails and download new ones  it was unbelievably freeing to not have  to load my laptop to get my emails and  to be able to reply at my leisure op  number-five Instapaper and Zeit usually  when I go on vacation I packed a lot of  books and magazines as reading material  this time my goal was to pack everything  I needed for the entire two-week trip in  one backpack and carry it with me books  and magazines are heavy so they couldn't  come with me  enter Instapaper Instapaper was after  the first app I bought when I got my  iPad what did it allows you to do is  clip articles that you read online and  save them to read offline later you can  install a little button on your browser  and whenever you see something that you  want to read but don't have the time yet  click the button it'll save it and you  can read it offline on your iPad  whenever you want I get a lot of my  reading material from the RSS feeds that  I subscribe to in Google Reader and  instapaper has built-in intelligence to  work with Google Reader so it's a  seamless process I also get my news from  site which is free which has instant  paper integration as part of my daily  routine in Toronto I'll go through my  Google Reader and Zeit while I eat  breakfast and save anything that's  interesting the instant paper then I'll  read it on my iPad as I walk to and from  work before leaving on this trip I  loaded up my instant paper with lots of  reading material from blogs that I  follow and when I connected to send  emails I often loaded up my site to save  any interesting articles as well it gave  me lots of reading material to go  through offline while relaxing on a deck  chair on the cruise ship and be carrying  around heavy books and magazines with me  everywhere  app number six interactive ebooks for  kids for those of you who travel with  kids I would definitely recommend  checking out some of the interactive  ebooks you can install on your iPad we  don't let our son watch TV yep and we  didn't have space to bring all his books  so I downloaded a number of e-books that  he thoroughly enjoyed while we were away  they were educational and also a great  way to calm him down when he was getting  too tired or worked up there are many  options out there but you have to sort  through them to find the good ones that  are age-appropriate my two-year-old  son's favorites were the monster at the  end of the book Thomas and Friends  Mickey spooky night puzzle book and the  Lorax for dr. Seuss they're all teach  reading skills and interactive and allow  your kids to explore books in a whole  new way as well as give their parents  some time to relax  up number seven maps when traveling in  the past I used to get a map of each  place we were visiting research all the  spots I wanted to visit and mark them on  a map the map would usually start to  wear down on me with all the folding and  unfolding throughout the course of the  day if we wanted to find something that  I didn't mark on the map we had to ask  the locals and hope they gave us the  right directions entered the native Maps  app maps is automatically installed on  your iPad and saved me so many times on  this trip it can automatically detect  where you are in a city and you can  quickly see where you have to go seen it  on the big screen was so much more  helpful than on the iPhone especially  when you're in a city as big as New York  and you want to cover a lot of territory  we use it to plan our subway routes look  up sushi restaurants see how far away we  were from our car find our cruise ship  and the list went on my favorite use was  when I was shopping in a drugstore in  New York City and a grandmother with her  baby grandchild asked me if there was a  Walgreens anywhere nearby my Toronto  Blue Jays hat didn't tip her off that I  was in a local I pulled up my iPad  searched Walgreens and maps and showed  her that there was one two blocks away  and how to get there she was floored and  it made her day number eight  GarageBand I purposely removed any games  I had on my iPad I tried many of them  out for a month and found them to be  overly addictive and counterproductive  better to delete them completely and not  be tempted but I found myself sometimes  wanting to have some fun in my downtime  instead of reading enter garage read I  started using GarageBand when YouTube  was giving me issues with having  background music in my videos even  though I had the rights to use the music  I'm currently uploading about 5 videos  per week on my youtube channel and each  one of them was a battle with YouTube of  the music rights so I decided to create  my own music and I use GarageBand to do  it the music you hear in the background  of this video was created by me in brush  man so when I found myself wanting to  have a little more fun I cranked open  GarageBand and started composing with  earphones on so it's not the disturbed  rest of my family  it's a great way to kill boredom but do  something in that somewhat practical  instead of playing games at least that's  what I told myself in conclusion the  trip was made so much easier and more  enjoyable because of the iPad we had  music we could travel lightly we could  sleep we knew where we were going and we  had a lot more fun being able to travel  without having used my computer was so  liberating  I can't imagine ever going back and  can't wait for my next trip thank you  for joining me for another video if you  guys liked it please give it a thumbs up  below I'd also love to hear your  thoughts and feedback if you want to  leave a comment under the video and stay  tuned for the next episode  you
 

